{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/942628-extra-action-with-rage-and-frenesi","id":942628,"title":"Extra Action with Rage and Frenesi","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-03T04:09:16-07:00","id":942628,"title":"Extra Action with Rage and Frenesi","content":"My friend Storyteller requires a frenzy test whenever a garou spend Rage points for further action in combat.<br /> <br /> But it always involves packs of players ending combat in Frenzy or duelists of klaive abandoning their weapons and leaving for a fight with claws and fangs.<br /> <br /> When I am the Storyteller I do not require these tests because I think this method weakens the use of Rage.<br /> <br /> I believe the frenzy test should only be performed when the characters are angry, hungry, humiliated, provoked or disturbed emotionally.<br /> <br /> For me Rage is the the channeling wrath, designed to transform it into a fighting machine, not necessarily a beast maddened in any combat.<br /> <br /> Which of the two interpretations is more correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12210,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","user":"Ulisses","date":". 08-03-2016, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T04:25:50-07:00","id":942631,"title":"","content":"Easy! W20 page 261<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Rage Rolls</b><br /> At the Storyteller\u2019s discretion, any of the following conditions may call for a Rage roll.<br /> \u2022 Embarrassment or humiliation (e.g. botching an important roll)<br /> \u2022 Any strong emotion (lust, rage, envy)<br /> \u2022 Extreme hunger<br /> \u2022 Confinement<br /> \u2022 Helplessness<br /> \u2022 Being taunted by a superior enemy<br /> \u2022 Large quantities of silver in the area<br /> \u2022 Being wounded<br /> \u2022 Seeing a packmate wounded </div> </div> </div>These are just the rolles that are solely made to check for frenzy. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any Rage roll can lead to a frenzy, even if it\u2019s used to activate Gifts. </div> </div> </div> and page 256's <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To remain active, the player rolls his character\u2019s permanent Rage (difficulty 8). Each success heals one health level of any kind of damage. No matter how much damage is healed, the character enters a berserk frenzy. </div> </div> </div> still apply.<br /> <br /> But no, not every Rage spend should trigger a frenzy check, just like not every trigger should regain Rage.<br /> <br /> If seen a lot of strange houserules on that, but usually having the whole troupe in frenzy is a total party kill, and that is not a story I'd like to tell...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T21:30:00-07:00","id":944118,"title":"","content":"I don't call for Frenzy simply for spending Rage.<br /> <br /> And I am fairly lenient at allowing players to spend Willpower to prevent Frenzy.<br /> <br /> If it is appropriate dramatically and storywise for Frenzy, I don't mind it. But it can easily derail the game. I try to keep it reasonable and fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}